# English-only in Git

Everything committed to this repository must be in **English**, unless an existing file is explicitly marked as a localized exception (none by default).

This includes:

- README, docs, comments aimed at readers, and commit messages on branches we manage
- Sample documents under `data/raw/` used for RAG and eval
- User-visible API strings, prompts, error messages, Makefile echo text, and workflow names
- Tests: names, docstrings, fixture data, and assertion messages

Do **not** add new Estonian or other non-English text to tracked files. Conversations with the user may stay in their language; **git content stays English**.

When editing existing non-English text in the repo, translate it to English as part of the same change.